<title>GERMANY: Linde buys unit of UK's Wagon Industrial.</title>
<headline>Linde buys unit of UK's Wagon Industrial.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>German engineering company Linde AG said on Wednesday it plans to buy a division of Britain's Wagon Industrial Plc on August 1 to strengthen its position in the British market for commercial freezers, refrigerators and shop fittings.</p>
<p>The purchase price for the division, called Radford Retail Systems, was not disclosed. The acquisition has yet to be approved by Wagon Industrial's shareholders, Linde said in a statement.</p>
<p>Radford Retail Systems has annual sales of 80.5 million pounds and is among the leading suppliers of supermarket equipment in Britain. It employs some 930 people.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
